cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this framework in research, experiments, or derivative work, please cite this repository."
title: "Principia Structurae Realitatis: A Structural Reasoning Framework for Whole-System Coordination in LLMs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "CosmicUndercurrent"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-22
repository-code: "https://github.com/CosmicUndercurrent/Principia-Structurae-Realitatis"
url: "https://github.com/CosmicUndercurrent/Principia-Structurae-Realitatis"
abstract: >-
  Principia Structurae Realitatis is an open research framework built around the structural expression
  Reality = Consciousness × Matter × Coordination. For AI use, the expression is treated as a
  generative reasoning seed rather than ordinary arithmetic. The public framework focuses on
  whole-system coordination, constraint retention, dependency propagation, contradiction detection,
  local-versus-global feasibility, reasoning-policy stability, and controlled A/B testing across LLMs.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM reasoning
  - coordination
  - whole-system reasoning
  - prompt engineering
  - constraint propagation
  - reasoning policy drift
  - artificial intelligence
